                <pb facs="0620" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.85/1127: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wallace</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-23T21:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                                1920—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 23—4:38
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1046. B–39 for Department and Davis.</p>
                <p>1st. Information received that French Government has agreed to full acceptance of
                    Wilson–Lloyd George Agreement. This acceptance was embodied in recent
                    Anglo-French shipping agreement signed in London April 22. Boyden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
